// The project manifest for the Cadenza choreographic-protocols library, written in Cadenza itself.
// `cdz` reads these well-known top-level defs to know how to build / run / test the project.
//
//   cdz test          — search up for this Project.cdz and run its suite (like cargo)
//   cdz test .        — same, naming this directory
//
// This is a SIDECAR package (operator ruling 2026-07-18): choreographic programming lives in its OWN
// package OUTSIDE compiler-ml so it does not distract the compiler-ml integer-spine initiative, and it
// targets the RUST compiler (rcdzc / `cdz`) so it works TODAY without waiting on the self-hosted compiler.
// Like the iterators / cad / agent-harness siblings, it is a self-contained package the rust `cdz` builds.
//
// It is prelude-only + self-contained: it vendors a minimal homoiconic `Ast` (src/ast.cdz, src/ast-eq.cdz)
// rather than depending on the compiler pipeline, so it has NO dependency on compiler-ml. The choreography
// AST, projectability analysis, projection to local types, code generation, mock-Comm execution, and the
// deadlock-freedom checker are all here.

def name = "choreography"

// Every source module under src/ (a wildcard, so a new module just drops into src/ and is picked up).
//   ast/ast-eq          — a vendored minimal homoiconic Ast (Int|Str|Bool|Name|List) + structural equality
//   chor                — the global-protocol AST + canonical round-trip + well-formedness
//   chor-project        — projectability / knowledge-of-choice analysis (the reject path)
//   chor-local          — projection to per-role local (session) types (project : Chor -> Role -> Local)
//   chor-codegen        — code generation from a local type to an actor program Ast (codegen : Local -> Ast)
//   chor-run            — execute generated actors over a destination-aware mock Comm medium
//   chor-safety         — deadlock-freedom by construction (matched-I/O checker)
//   chor-fleet          — the flagship: the fleet's own coordination as a choreography (FleetIntegrate)
//   chor-consistency    — cross-pass coverage (project <-> codegen <-> run agree)
//   chor-diag           — actionable projectability diagnostics
def modules = ["src/*.cdz"]

// The modules whose `@test` definitions form the suite. Same-file with their code.
def tests = ["src/*.cdz"]

// Files removed from the globs above. Empty — every src/*.cdz is a real module.
def exclude = []
